          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "CDIAL lists દાઢી (dāḍhī), \"beard, chin\", under a reconstructed dāṁṣṭra, \"fang, tusk, beard\", beside Sanskrit daṁṣṭra, \"tusk, fang\" (CDIAL 6250). It holds that the sense could move from \"fang\" to \"beard\", and does not rule out some Dravidian or Munda influence."
            }
          ]
        },
